WEBVTT

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:06.510
Last episode, the Darkling Lord set about capturing the good knights of Prismos one by one.

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:09.730
Hold tight!

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:14.070
First, the evil Verulina, disguised as a fair maiden,

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:17.510
lured the unsuspecting Arzon into a dangerous trap.

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:19.690
Attack!

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:29.620
With the aid of magical vehicles driven by Mordred and Recon,

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:34.360
The Darkling lords hunted down Winterquick and the mighty Cryotech.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.020
Can't hold his bare form much longer.

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:40.100
Now, chain him!

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:44.620
Put him aboard.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:49.820
Galadriel managed to escape and warn Leoric of Darkstorm's treachery.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:54.360
I'm sorry to disturb your festivities,

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:57.440
but Cryotech has been captured by Darkstorm and his knights.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:59.940
Now, this is what comes of peace treaty.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.880
with dark storm the parapets must be manned at all times we can expect a vicious onslaught

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:11.540
but before leora could take action the darkling lords lay siege to his castle

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:16.470
and the remaining good knights were conquered and thrown into a deep dungeon

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:22.890
there they agreed to form a sacred brotherhood called the spectral knights

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:29.980
remember the wisdom given to me by my power staff yes something cryptic about becoming one with the

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:37.160
circle of light i propose that right now we form the spectral knights a sacred order dedicated to

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:44.840
bringing light to the darkness of our world may the light shine forever may the light shine

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:55.360
forever but was this too little and too late see how your light shines under water

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:04.490
So, Darkstrom, how are we going to divide the booty?

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:06.680
Divide the booty?

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:09.250
What insolence!

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:14.080
I am your lord and ruler who swore loyalty to me.

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:16.280
The spoils are mine.

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:17.820
All mine.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:18.820
One moment.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:21.000
Swearing loyalty is one thing.

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:24.690
Turning over all my money to you is quite another.

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:29.970
Apologize now, and I will not subject you to my...

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.580
All that work and we get nothing?

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:35.620
I hardly think that's fair. We could die paupers.

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:37.600
What did you say, Lexor?

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:41.220
I just said that I was shocked by recons in subordination.

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:47.530
You expect to enrage me into doing your dirty work?

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:49.570
Well, you have succeeded.

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:51.400
You enraged me?

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:54.870
Greedy swine!

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:59.090
What gives you the right to lay claim to the fruits of our labor?

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:04.070
Lying filth! You are a mercenary!

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.830
You have no loyalty.

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:09.210
For enough money, you would betray yourself!

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:13.910
You, Mothred! Boot licker!

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:15.950
Have you no will of your own?

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:20.420
Sindar, I'll just crack you out of principle!

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:23.180
Restrain him!

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:26.060
Not until I'm compensated!

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:29.370
Oh no!

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:38.190
much longer i can keep treading water i have an idea i'll fly up with leoric and we'll come back down

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:39.210
and get you

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:01.230
SHUT!

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:08.660
How could you let him get away?

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:15.020
M****s have escaped after them!

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:19.140
Wait a minute!

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:21.010
You were in that cell!

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:50.070
Let's get Feral his magical totem back, then get our weapons and round up Darkstorm at his cronies.

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.170
Isn't that a little over-ambitious?

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:54.620
Perhaps, but it's worth a try.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:04.980
What's going on?

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:06.720
Dark Storm's given orders.

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.520
Nobody's to touch the dagger assault.

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:10.840
Oh, allow me to make your acquaintance.

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:12.160
I am Sir Ace McGillicuddy.

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:12.840
Magical Repairs?

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:15.800
I'm having a devil of a time repairing this magical dungeon.

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:17.340
Perhaps you could help me out.

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:19.980
I have more important things to attend to.

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:29.850
I hope the others are having the same success.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:37.940
the armory when dark storm finds out about this he will dangle you from your heels probably and

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:45.400
what do you suppose he'll do to you oh i hadn't considered that why do you question the rightful

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:51.520
rule of dark storm king of the cliffs baron of the bog marsh why do you not answer me

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:57.010
to be true for once i agree

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:06.190
What creeps, what crawls, by what does not, let all that grows, recede and rot!

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:09.800
It's useless!

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:19.050
Destruction! Knowledge! Wisdom! Fear! Speed! Useless!

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:23.270
Sorry, Darkstorm, but Merklin warned you of their limits.

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:26.880
You must return to the shrine to recharge them.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:29.580
And we'll make sure that never happens.

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:32.440
Recon! Evacuate us!

00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:34.310
Darkling lords!

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:35.590
To the vehicles!

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:47.630
If Recon and Mortred can activate vehicles,

00:06:47.930 --> 00:06:49.690
my guess is that you can too.

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:54.640
Here goes nothing!

00:06:57.230 --> 00:06:58.590
What should I do?

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:07.300
I love one of these.

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:08.160
Don't worry.

00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:09.320
All right, then.

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:10.780
I'll just hang on for the...

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:14.660
We're going to hit the wall!

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:29.890
Chris.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.870
Still alive and still very dangerous.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:04.610
Dark Storm, what will rescue you?

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:09.750
Nothing compared to what you will pay if you don't stop this thing.

00:09:10.220 --> 00:09:12.560
There is no profit in resisting.

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:17.530
Work, Leoric. The Darkling laws are finished.

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:21.370
Dark Storm's reign of tyranny is over,

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:25.530
and all property is returned to all men.

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:40.490
This will spring you from your bones.

00:09:41.750 --> 00:09:43.510
Thank you, Mirklin.

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:09.100
Dark Stormer, may I suggest, allow me to do your work for you.

00:10:09.590 --> 00:10:16.110
Surely it is not right for one of your great power and awesome majesty to waste his time making traffic signs.

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:21.910
Hmm, true. I do find this work personally degrading.

00:10:22.280 --> 00:10:29.980
That's because it is degrading. And I have no pity for you. It is your fault. We are in there.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.480
This terrible predicament.

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:38.060
Dark Storm, it is wretched here.

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:41.330
Why don't you just use that key Merklin gave you?

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:45.630
Because it is my decision to save it for when we truly need it.

00:10:46.110 --> 00:10:48.390
I'd say we truly need it now.

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:52.470
I have heard there are agricultural difficulties.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:55.820
We've come here to the fields to see how we can be of assistance.

00:10:56.520 --> 00:10:59.860
If we don't get relief soon, well, the farms.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:03.160
and then New Valaric are going to wither away.

00:11:03.460 --> 00:11:05.240
What can the Spectral Knights do to help?

00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:07.540
The fact is, we don't know.

00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:09.180
We've watered it.

00:11:09.380 --> 00:11:10.940
Oh, we've spread fertilizer.

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:12.920
And still nothing grows.

00:11:13.320 --> 00:11:16.700
Shucks, we'd do a rain dance if we thought it would do some good.

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:19.310
Fact is, we're all out of ideas.

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:22.440
The problems might have something to do with a new age.

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:24.600
Perhaps we should go to Merklin for advice.

00:11:24.940 --> 00:11:28.820
Yes, maybe he'll let us trade in the Darkling Lord's power staffs

00:11:28.820 --> 00:11:29.960
for a magical cure.

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:32.060
It's worth a try.

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:35.820
We will set out tomorrow and we will not return without a solution.

00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:38.740
I will stay behind to guard the Darkling Lords.

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:49.140
Pathetic! You forced me to use the key!

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:52.770
I wonder what I'd do with it.

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:55.400
You course, Pathetic!

00:11:57.490 --> 00:11:59.630
I guess you don't have to do anything.

00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:07.900
It was a mark of a great leader to promise your people you would not return until you have solved their problems

00:12:07.900 --> 00:12:13.490
If I don't solve the problems, there will be nothing to return to. What do you mean vanished?

00:12:14.180 --> 00:12:19.610
Well, we came in and they just kind of weren't here. We're sorry.

00:12:20.150 --> 00:12:24.660
The blame rests on my shoulders. I should never have let them out of my sight.

00:12:28.210 --> 00:12:29.980
Yes, this is a much better...

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:39.100
nicer journey now that there aren't a lot of surprises popping up to my command let loose the

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:46.440
avalanche you know it might be a good idea to build an elevator to the shrine ready ready then

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:52.690
we could avoid this all together i second that motion and how would we power an elevator well

00:12:52.690 --> 00:12:58.310
i was thinking we could have oxen in the valley and spectral lights bewuggling

00:13:01.810 --> 00:13:02.850
That's Hector

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:06.180
Lose the avalanche

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:25.650
I'll burn

00:13:30.350 --> 00:13:31.850
Our power staffs.

00:13:33.230 --> 00:13:47.540
The wickling lords disappeared as quickly as they came.

00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:48.620
Thank you, Hector.

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:51.550
Were it not for you, we'd be dead.

00:13:51.900 --> 00:13:55.520
The truth is, I failed in my mission to contain them in the prison.

00:13:55.840 --> 00:13:56.800
I doubt that.

00:13:57.230 --> 00:13:59.570
I sense the hand of magic in their escape.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:03.070
Well, enough talk. Let us head for the shrine.

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:08.910
So, you have come to rekindle your magic.

00:14:09.470 --> 00:14:15.390
Yes, I am afraid we have spent it defending ourselves against the evil spectral knights.

00:14:15.730 --> 00:14:16.330
Rubbish!

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:18.960
Let us settle this dispute forever!

00:14:19.470 --> 00:14:19.770
Right!

00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:24.610
There will be no fighting in the shrine!

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:27.110
Let me be clear on this point.

00:14:27.940 --> 00:14:29.960
I care nothing for your petty...

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:37.430
wobbles. I have concerns of my own. Now, if you wish more magic, you will venture on a quest for

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:45.030
the Dragon's Eye. Dragon's Eye? Silence! Do you think I give you magic out of selflessness?

00:14:45.710 --> 00:14:54.550
Of course not. I do it because I want you to be instrument of my will. But to show that I intend

00:14:54.550 --> 00:14:59.800
to be fair, I will allow you to dip your power stuffs into the sacred pool.

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:14.240
one last time for free now here is your map we shall return with the dragon's eye and why have

00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:23.060
you stayed behind because we refuse your demands darkling lords attack by nature's hand by craft

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:26.580
by art but once was one now fly apart

00:15:26.580 --> 00:15:29.970
It's true, it's dark and clear.

00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:41.060
By what creeps, what crawls, by what does not, let all that grows, recede and rot!

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:52.450
Do you wish of me? Carry him!

00:15:53.060 --> 00:15:58.870
I cannot attack the holder of the orb!

00:16:04.570 --> 00:16:07.630
Well, then, we shall attack him ourselves!

00:16:08.770 --> 00:16:18.100
It had nothing to do with Storm's plot, please!

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:22.480
Dead coward, important things must be done.

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:26.240
Now, get me the dragon's eye.

00:16:29.280 --> 00:16:29.740
Well...

00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:30.820
We're here.

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:33.820
Foogey.

00:16:34.320 --> 00:16:36.260
Just an old industrial complex.

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:37.840
Wait, what was that?

00:16:39.860 --> 00:16:44.280
I feared it's something spawned by this age of magic that we do not know yet.

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:48.800
Better to venture forward than to be caught from behind by the Darkling Lords.

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:51.080
It's a bit late for that.

00:16:51.420 --> 00:16:53.300
Cinder, release your beast.

00:16:53.560 --> 00:16:55.860
By nature's hand, by craft, by art.

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:58.380
What once was won, now fly apart.

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:07.620
There's some nasty magic here.

00:17:14.430 --> 00:17:18.090
Speak to Merklin about an obedience school for that beast.

00:17:18.810 --> 00:17:19.690
In there!

00:17:20.050 --> 00:17:23.590
Don't let them get ahead of us!

00:17:27.270 --> 00:17:29.440
A techno-dragon.

00:17:31.370 --> 00:17:33.630
And that must be the dragon's eye.

00:17:33.790 --> 00:17:35.010
But who's holding it?

00:17:35.390 --> 00:17:37.070
Why don't you ask your knowledge staff?

00:17:37.390 --> 00:17:39.850
A whim, a thought, and more is sought.

00:17:40.010 --> 00:17:42.050
Awake, my mind, thy will be wrought.

00:17:42.930 --> 00:17:45.540
What do you wish to know?

00:17:46.020 --> 00:17:47.060
Who is that up there?

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:49.320
He is the wizard Volcarma,

00:17:49.640 --> 00:17:52.200
believed until recently to be legendary.

00:17:52.900 --> 00:17:56.340
Volcarma was in the same circle of wizardry as Merklin,

00:17:57.220 --> 00:17:59.220
Bogavus, Wisesquizar, and others.

00:18:00.280 --> 00:18:02.500
No, dragon. Smite them.

00:18:04.690 --> 00:18:14.100
Get big.

00:18:18.770 --> 00:18:19.930
You think I stop it?

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:21.020
Don't answer that.

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:23.660
I think we'll have a better chance in the incinerator.

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:25.080
Our armor's heat resistant.

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:26.580
And let's jump forward.

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:29.960
Three seconds.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:34.580
The sun's aligned, pour forth their light, and fill the answer's bow with might!

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:41.410
If you could make the dragon feel fear!

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:43.760
I owe you no such favor!

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:45.520
Then you owe it to yourself!

00:18:45.900 --> 00:18:49.820
Perhaps you're right. Oh, mist-filled pits, dark, dank, unclear!

00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:52.780
Touch all before me with frost-fingered fear!

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:57.840
A Murglin gave them too great a power!

00:19:16.030 --> 00:19:16.490
For long.

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:18.680
Sheet these feet in the driving gale.

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:20.920
Make swift these legs or land I sail.

00:19:24.940 --> 00:19:26.200
And over the dragon's eye.

00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:27.910
Get it!

00:19:28.070 --> 00:19:28.610
Watch out!

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:52.130
I get it by incompetence.

00:19:54.220 --> 00:19:55.920
Did you bring the dragon's eye?

00:19:56.220 --> 00:19:56.860
We did.

00:19:57.140 --> 00:19:57.560
Good.

00:19:58.400 --> 00:19:59.920
I will charge your power star.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:07.940
once more i'm sorry that's not good enough what do you mean by that insolence look we know you need

00:20:07.940 --> 00:20:14.420
the dragon's eye without it the sacred pool will lose its magical power all right i will give you

00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:21.070
magic to help your cities but never tell the darkling lords of the power you have wielded

00:20:21.070 --> 00:20:25.200
over me believe me we are not so stupid here

00:20:31.690 --> 00:20:33.790
Find this guy sneaking out.

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:35.040
Discard him.

00:20:35.180 --> 00:20:37.260
But I can be of great use to you.

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:40.920
I know things of magic and of Merkland that can help you.

00:20:41.230 --> 00:20:43.870
Put him with the rest of the things we have scavenged.

00:20:44.310 --> 00:20:46.490
Maybe we shall have use for him later.

00:20:48.960 --> 00:20:50.980
Leoric, I know nothing of farming.

00:20:51.420 --> 00:20:53.590
That's the beauty of this magic.

00:20:54.140 --> 00:20:55.100
You don't have to.

00:20:55.640 --> 00:20:58.300
So how long we gotta wait to see if this works?

00:21:03.610 --> 00:21:06.410
Well, Merklin said it would take just a few minutes.

00:21:30.800 --> 00:21:31.000
You
